      "num": "01",
      "en": "课文讲述北京高中生陈伟（Chen Wei）在餐馆用海姆立克急救法救助噎食者张涛（Zhang Tao）的故事，并介绍海姆立克急救法的操作步骤。课本要求将 A-E 五个句子填入课文适当位置，正确顺序为 **C → A → B → E → D**。 Chen Wei, a high school student in Beijing, had his dinner interrupted when he heard someone screaming from another table. A {fellow} {diner} at the restaurant, Zhang Tao, was choking on some {steak}. He was now holding his {throat} with his face turning red, while his {desperate} friends were slapping him on the back. **[C] Chen wasted no time.** He got up and ran to Zhang's table at once. With the help of Zhang's friends, he was able to help Zhang to his feet. Then, standing behind Zhang, Chen did the Heimlich manoeuvre. The food was instantly forced out, and Zhang began to breathe again. Ten minutes later, an {ambulance} arrived. The doctors checked Zhang and made sure that he was fine. They suggested he eat more slowly and take smaller bites before they left. **[A] Choking victims usually have only about four minutes before they {collapse} and sometimes die.** Leaving no time for an {ambulance} to arrive. To solve this problem, in 1974, an American doctor, Henry Heimlich, created the Heimlich manoeuvre, which is so easy that almost anyone can learn how. **[B] If you see someone choking, first call the emergency services.** Then, make sure that the {victim} is really choking: A choking person cannot speak. Slapping the {victim}'s back will often force out the {obstruction}. If this does not work, you can perform the Heimlich manoeuvre by standing behind the {victim} and wrapping your arms around his waist. Make a {fist} with one hand and place it in the upper part of his stomach. Grabbing your {fist} with your other hand tightly, push up and into his stomach in one {motion}. Continue doing this until the {obstruction} is forced out. **[E] Doing the Heimlich manoeuvre on a small child is not recommended**, as you may hurt him. Instead, lay the child face down on your lap with the head lower than the rest of his body, and then give firm slaps to his upper back until he can breathe again. **[D] With choking victims, every minute counts.** You cannot just stand by and do nothing. Luckily, Chen had learnt how to give first aid in school. He had taken part in a first-aid training course organised by the Red Cross. Knowing how to perform first-aid techniques, such as the Heimlich manoeuvre, can mean the difference between life and death.",
      "cn": "陈伟是北京的一名高中生。他正在吃晚饭，突然听到另一桌有人尖叫。同在一家餐馆用餐的张涛被牛排噎住了。张涛抓着自己的喉咙，脸涨得通红，而他焦急的朋友们正在拍打他的后背。 **[C] 陈伟没有浪费任何时间。** 他立刻起身跑向张涛的桌子。在张涛朋友们的帮助下，他把张涛扶了起来。然后，陈伟站在张涛身后，实施了海姆立克急救法。食物立刻被挤压了出来，张涛又开始呼吸了。十分钟后，救护车到了。医生们检查了张涛，确认他安然无恙。离开前，他们建议他吃慢一点，小口进食。 **[A] 噎食者通常只有大约四分钟的时间，之后就会昏倒，有时甚至会死亡。** 根本来不及等救护车到达。为了解决这个问题，1974 年，美国医生亨利·海姆立克发明了海姆立克急救法，这种方法非常简单，几乎人人都可以学会。 **[B] 如果你看到有人噎住了，首先拨打急救电话。** 然后，确认伤者是否真的噎住了：噎住的人无法说话。拍打伤者的后背通常能将堵塞物挤压出来。如果这不起作用，你可以实施海姆立克急救法：站在伤者身后，用双臂环抱住他的腰部。一只手握拳，放在他上腹部的位置。另一只手紧紧抓住拳头，用力向上向内推压腹部。持续重复这个动作，直到堵塞物被挤压出来。 **[E] 不建议对幼童实施海姆立克急救法**，因为你可能会伤到他。取而代之的是，让孩子面朝下趴在你的腿上，头部低于身体其他部位，然后用力拍打他的上背部，直到他能重新呼吸。 **[D] 对于噎食者来说，分秒必争。** 你不能袖手旁观，什么都不做。幸运的是，陈伟在学校学过如何进行急救。他参加过红十字会组织的急救培训课程。懂得如何实施急救技术，比如海姆立克急救法，可能意味着生与死的差别。"
    }
  ],
